From 57d96314750c9e4cbcb7b80e08c8a01dafc123cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:17:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Keep paths from Lua inside the game, and ToPBR behind the
 player's settings (R19)

Any server's client Lua reaches this module's Lua functions. A path it names reached the disk
outside the game, or another host: a UNC path makes Windows open an SMB session and offer the
player's Windows login (the pre-release review's H3).

- source/lua_path_policy.h (SDK-free): a relative game path has no drive, root, UNC or "\\?\"
  prefix, no ':', no ".." segment, no shortened or device segment and no control character; a
  model file is on a local drive; a folder stays inside its root after lexical normalisation.
- MaterialPipeline.ToPBR.SetOutputDirectory takes a folder relative to the converter's own,
  <game>\rtx-remix\mods\~gmod_topbr\textures, rechecks the resolved folder and refuses links
  below it; it warns, keeps the folder and returns false otherwise (true when taken).
- ToPBR's switches follow the player's convars, read from the engine's list: SetEnabled(true)
  takes effect only while rtx_topbr_enabled is 1 and SetGameEnabled(true) only while
  rtx_topbr_game_maps is 1; PumpSnapshots turns either off within 250 ms of the player doing so;
  ProcessSingleMaterial, ConvertTexture and the queueing bindings check rtx_topbr_enabled.
- QueueGameMaterial and GameMaterialAction treat a source that is not a PMX on a local drive, and
  model paths that leave its folder, as absent; recorded maps still restore by texture identity.
- The game's file system opens absolute and network paths as they are: VTFParser::ReadVTFFile,
  ToPBR's VMT reader and auto-categorisation's VMT shader reader read only relative game paths.
- RemixMaterial's texture paths and RemixLight's dome colorTexture must be relative to the game
  folder (a Lua error otherwise); RemixConfig.SetConfigVariable refuses the options whose value
  Remix opens or loads code from (textures, the camera sequence file, NRC's CUDA DLL folder,
  Nsight's folders, capture names, the mod redirect) and any value naming a drive, root or
  network path.
- Tests: tests/lua_path_policy_test.cpp (SDK-free), tests/vtf_parser/test.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
